<%#
  Taking a domain off its hosting.

  ONE CARD FOR THREE CASES, because the wording is the whole feature and three
  copies of it in three templates would disagree within a month:

    ours       registered through us. The registration is paid for and stays;
               only the hosting goes. The plan it was on goes back to having no
               domain attached, and nothing else about the plan changes.
    subdomain  a name under a domain on this account. Nothing else holds it, so
               removing it removes it.
    external   registered elsewhere and pointed here. Same — the row goes, the
               domain itself is somebody else's registry entry and untouched.

  THE CHECKBOXES ARE THE POINT for the first case. `v-delete-domain` takes the
  website, the DNS zone and the mail domain together, and for a domain delegated
  to our nameservers that zone is the only reason the name resolves at all —
  removing a site should not silently take the domain off the internet and
  delete its mailboxes on the way. So each part that actually exists on the
  server is offered separately, with what is in it, and unticked stays.

  Expects: domain, node (from linking.nodeState), ours, parentName.
%>
<div class="p-card">
  <h2 class="h3 mb-2"><%= ours ? 'Remove from hosting' : 'Remove this ' + (domain.source === 'subdomain' ? 'subdomain' : 'domain') %></h2>

  <% if (ours) { %>
    <p class="small muted mb-2">
      Takes <span class="mono"><%= domain.domain %></span> off its hosting plan and deletes its
      website and files from our server. <b>The registration is not affected</b> — the domain
      stays yours, keeps its renewal date, and you can attach it to a plan again at any time.
    </p>
  <% } else if (domain.source === 'subdomain') { %>
    <p class="small muted mb-2">
      Deletes the site, its files and its certificate from our server.
      <b><%= parentName || 'The main domain' %> is not affected.</b>
      You can add the subdomain again at any time.
    </p>
  <% } else { %>
    <p class="small muted mb-2">
      Takes <span class="mono"><%= domain.domain %></span> off your Vesopa account and stops us
      hosting it, along with its website, DNS and mail here. The domain itself is registered
      elsewhere and is not affected in any way — you can add it back at any time.
    </p>
  <% } %>

  <form method="post" action="/panel/domains/<%= domain.domain %>/remove" data-guard
        data-confirm="Remove <%= domain.domain %> from <%= ours ? 'its hosting plan' : 'your account' %>? Its website and files are deleted from the server and cannot be recovered.">
    <input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="<%= csrf %>">

    <% if (ours && (node.dns || node.mail)) { %>
      <p class="label mb-1">We also run these for <%= domain.domain %></p>
      <p class="tiny muted mb-2">
        Tick anything you want deleted as well. Leave them and they keep working —
        the domain simply has no website here.
      </p>

      <% if (node.dns) { %>
        <label class="check">
          <input type="checkbox" name="drop_dns" value="1">
          <span>
            <span class="strong">DNS<% if (node.dnsRecords) { %> — <%= node.dnsRecords %> record<%= node.dnsRecords === 1 ? '' : 's' %><% } %></span>
            <span class="tiny muted" style="display:block">
              Deletes the zone we answer for. <b>Only do this if you are moving DNS elsewhere first</b> —
              while the domain is delegated to our nameservers, deleting the zone stops the name
              resolving anywhere at all, email included.
            </span>
          </span>
        </label>
      <% } %>

      <% if (node.mail) { %>
        <label class="check">
          <input type="checkbox" name="drop_mail" value="1">
          <span>
            <span class="strong">Email<% if (node.mailboxes) { %> — <%= node.mailboxes %> mailbox<%= node.mailboxes === 1 ? '' : 'es' %><% } %></span>
            <span class="tiny muted" style="display:block">
              Stops us accepting mail for this domain<%= node.mailboxes ? ' and deletes the mailboxes and everything in them' : '' %>.
              This cannot be undone.
            </span>
          </span>
        </label>
      <% } %>
    <% } %>

    <button class="btn btn-ghost btn-sm" type="submit" data-busy="Removing…">
      <%= ours ? 'Remove from hosting' : 'Remove ' + domain.domain %>
    </button>
  </form>
</div>
